masters-wheel is a prototype of "Master's Circle" — a mastery platform where
lessons and videos get uploaded, performance gets analyzed, and the system
always points back to the right lesson to refocus on. Nothing above the UI
shell is built yet.

This INIT phase builds no features. It only picks the stack (Next.js App
Router, TypeScript, CSS Modules, no component library) and establishes the
element architecture: every UI element is its own folder of a component file,
a styling file, and a positioning file (styling = how it looks, positioning =
where it sits within its parent), plus an optional script file and an
optional children/ folder for sub-elements that aren't reused elsewhere.
Reusable elements (e.g. a standardized side-menu button) are imported wherever
they're needed rather than duplicated.

Status: scaffolded 2026-10-27. `src/elements/Canvas/` is the root element and
doubles as the reference example of the convention — see CLAUDE.md.

Generate Transcript (added later) needs `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` for cloud
transcription — the one secret in `.env` so far.
